<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><%- include('../partials/head', { title, appName, seo: typeof seo !== 'undefined' ? seo : undefined }) %></head>
<body data-force-theme="dark">
    <main class="landing-shell sr-legal">
        <nav class="landing-nav sr-nav">
            <a class="brand" href="/" style="padding:0"><%- include('../partials/brand-logo') %></a>
            <div class="landing-nav-links">
                <a href="/">Home</a>
                <a href="/#pricing">Pricing</a>
                <a href="/demo">Demo</a>
                <a href="/faqs">FAQ</a>
                <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
            </div>
            <div class="toolbar-actions landing-nav-actions"><a class="button" href="/sign-in">Sign in</a><a class="button primary" href="/sign-up">Create account</a></div>
            <button class="landing-menu-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false" data-landing-menu-toggle>
                <span></span><span></span><span></span>
            </button>
            <div class="landing-mobile-menu" data-landing-menu>
                <a href="/">Home</a>
                <a href="/#pricing">Pricing</a>
                <a href="/demo">Demo</a>
                <a href="/faqs">FAQ</a>
                <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
                <div class="landing-mobile-actions">
                    <a class="button" href="/sign-in">Sign in</a>
                    <a class="button primary" href="/sign-up">Create account</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </nav>
        <section class="sr-legal-hero">
            <p class="sr-kicker">Legal center</p>
            <h1><%= legalTitle %></h1>
            <p>Policies for SecureRepos accounts, GitHub App access, billing, repository scanning, privacy, and support.</p>
            <div class="sr-legal-meta">
                <span><strong>Support</strong><a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a></span>
                <span><strong>Website</strong><a href="<%= websiteUrl %>"><%= websiteUrl %></a></span>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="sr-legal-layout">
            <aside class="sr-legal-sidebar">
                <span>Documents</span>
                <a href="/terms" class="<%= legalSlug === 'terms' ? 'active' : '' %>">Terms</a>
                <a href="/privacy" class="<%= legalSlug === 'privacy' ? 'active' : '' %>">Privacy</a>
                <a href="/refund-policy" class="<%= legalSlug === 'refund-policy' ? 'active' : '' %>">Refund Policy</a>
                <a href="/do-not-sell" class="<%= legalSlug === 'do-not-sell' ? 'active' : '' %>">Do Not Sell/Share</a>
            </aside>
            <div class="sr-legal-document">
        <% if (legalSlug === 'terms') { %>
            <section class="sr-legal-content">
                <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
                <p>By visiting the website, creating an account, selecting a plan, installing the GitHub App, or using <%= appName %>, you agree to these Terms and Conditions, the Privacy Policy, Refund Policy, and any checkout or billing disclosures presented at the time of purchase.</p>
                <p><%= appName %> is operated by Secure Repos. In these Terms, "we," "us," and "our" refer to Secure Repos and <%= appName %>. "You" and "user" refer to the person or organization using the service.</p>
                <h2>2. Service Description</h2>
                <p><%= appName %> provides repository security monitoring for individual GitHub users. Features may include repository inventory, automated scans, secret and configuration checks, GitHub Actions checks, dependency and container hygiene checks, finding review, notifications, account activity, and related security workflow tools.</p>
                <p>The service is a software tool. It is not a managed penetration test, legal service, incident response service, or guarantee that your repositories are secure.</p>
                <h2>3. Accounts and Access</h2>
                <p>You are responsible for the accuracy of account information, the security of login credentials, and all activity under your account. You must be authorized to connect the GitHub organizations, accounts, and repositories you add to <%= appName %>.</p>
                <p>You may not share credentials, bypass plan limits, reverse engineer the service, interfere with platform security, scan repositories you are not authorized to access, or use the service for unlawful activity.</p>
                <h2>4. GitHub App Connections</h2>
                <p>When you install the GitHub App, you authorize <%= appName %> to access selected repository metadata and repository content needed to perform scans, generate findings, and track repository status. You should select only repositories that you want monitored under your plan.</p>
                <p>You may revoke GitHub App access from GitHub. If access is revoked, suspended, or reduced, scans and repository updates may stop or become incomplete.</p>
                <h2>5. Plans and Billing</h2>
                <p>Pricing, billing interval, included repositories, usage limits, and plan features are displayed before purchase. Payment processing is handled by the checkout provider shown at payment. By completing checkout, you authorize the applicable charges shown at purchase.</p>
                <p>Where a 7-day Security Preview is offered, a payment method is required. The preview is limited to one repository and one non-comprehensive scan. Unless you cancel before the displayed trial end, the checkout provider will charge the recurring package price and the paid subscription will begin automatically.</p>
                <p>If your plan is offered as a subscription, it renews until cancelled according to the checkout terms. Access may be paused, limited, or terminated if payment fails, a charge is disputed, the plan is cancelled, or the account violates these Terms.</p>
                <p>The first GitHub account connected to a SecureRepos account is permanently bound to that account. Removing the GitHub App does not reset that binding or create a right to connect a different GitHub account.</p>
                <h2>6. Security Findings</h2>
                <p>Findings are generated by automated rules and may include false positives, incomplete results, or missed issues. Severity labels are guidance only. You remain responsible for reviewing results, validating risk, applying fixes, and deciding whether additional security review is needed.</p>
                <h2>7. Customer Data and Repository Content</h2>
                <p>Your repository content, organization data, and account data remain yours. You grant us the limited rights needed to operate the service, process scans, generate findings, deliver notifications, provide support, maintain security, and comply with legal obligations.</p>
                <h2>8. Intellectual Property</h2>
                <p><%= appName %>, its interface, scanner logic, branding, documentation, and platform materials are owned by Secure Repos or its licensors. You receive a limited, non-transferable right to use the service for your internal business purposes according to your plan.</p>
                <h2>9. Availability and Changes</h2>
                <p>We may update, improve, suspend, or discontinue parts of the service. We work to keep the platform reliable, but we do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free access.</p>
                <h2>10. Limitation of Liability</h2>
                <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, Secure Repos and <%= appName %> are not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, including lost profits, lost data, security incidents, repository compromise, or business interruption.</p>
                <h2>11. Governing Law</h2>
                <p>These Terms are governed by the laws applicable to Secure Repos, unless mandatory consumer protection laws require otherwise.</p>
                <h2>12. Contact</h2>
                <p>For account, billing, or legal questions, contact <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>
            </section>
        <% } else if (legalSlug === 'privacy') { %>
            <section class="sr-legal-content">
                <h2>1. Overview</h2>
                <p>This Privacy Policy explains how Secure Repos and <%= appName %> collect, use, disclose, and protect information when you visit the website, create an account, connect GitHub repositories, use scans, contact support, or interact with our services.</p>
                <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
                <p>We may collect account information such as name, email address, password hash, notification preferences, support messages, billing status, and plan information.</p>
                <p>We may also collect technical and product information such as IP address, browser, device data, login sessions, audit logs, page activity, repository IDs, repository names, default branches, GitHub App installation metadata, scan status, findings, and error logs.</p>
                <h2>3. Repository Data</h2>
                <p>Repository access is used to run security checks, create findings, track repository health, and support workflow features. Depending on the scan, <%= appName %> may process repository file paths, selected file contents, configuration files, dependency files, workflow files, and detected patterns. Temporary scanner workspaces are intended to be removed after scan output is parsed; finding metadata and scan history remain stored for your account.</p>
                <p>We do not sell repository code. You control repository access through the GitHub App installation and should limit access to repositories you want monitored.</p>
                <h2>4. How We Use Information</h2>
                <p>We use information to create and operate accounts, authenticate users, connect GitHub, run scans, generate findings, send emails and in-app notifications, enforce plan limits, improve reliability, prevent abuse, investigate errors, respond to support requests, process billing status, and comply with legal obligations.</p>
                <h2>5. Service Providers</h2>
                <p>We may use trusted providers for hosting, databases, infrastructure, email delivery, analytics, logging, security monitoring, payment processing, fraud prevention, and customer support. These providers process information only as needed to provide services to us.</p>
                <p>For dependency vulnerability checks, package names, exact versions, ecosystems, and dependency file paths may be sent to a vulnerability intelligence provider. Repository source code and dependency file contents are not sent for this lookup.</p>
                <h2>6. Cookies and Analytics</h2>
                <p>We use cookies and similar technologies for login sessions, security, preferences, product analytics, fraud prevention, and performance measurement. You can control cookies through browser settings, but some features may not work correctly if required cookies are blocked.</p>
                <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
                <p>We retain information while your account is active and as needed for security, audit, legal, billing, dispute, tax, backup, and operational purposes. Some records may be retained after cancellation where required for compliance, fraud prevention, dispute handling, or legitimate business records.</p>
                <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
                <p>Depending on your location, you may request access, correction, deletion, portability, restriction, or opt-out of certain processing. We may verify your identity before processing a request.</p>
                <h2>9. Security</h2>
                <p>We use reasonable operational, technical, and organizational safeguards designed to protect information. No online service is completely secure, and you are responsible for managing GitHub permissions and account access carefully.</p>
                <h2>10. International Processing</h2>
                <p>Your information may be processed in countries where we or our service providers operate. By using the service, you understand that information may be transferred and processed outside your country of residence where permitted by law.</p>
                <h2>11. Contact</h2>
                <p>For privacy requests, contact <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>
            </section>
        <% } else if (legalSlug === 'refund-policy') { %>
            <section class="sr-legal-content">
                <h2>1. Digital Service Refund Policy</h2>
                <p><%= appName %> is a digital SaaS product operated by Secure Repos. Once an account is activated and service access is delivered, fees are generally non-refundable unless required by law or approved by support.</p>
                <h2>2. Refund Requests</h2>
                <p>Refund requests are reviewed case by case. To request review, contact <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a> with your account email, purchase date, transaction reference if available, and reason for the request.</p>
                <h2>3. Billing Errors</h2>
                <p>If you believe you were charged incorrectly, contact support as soon as possible. Confirmed duplicate charges or billing errors may be corrected to the original payment method.</p>
                <h2>4. Cancellations</h2>
                <p>You may cancel during the Security Preview to prevent the first paid charge, subject to the cancellation status shown by Paddle. After paid billing begins, cancellation stops future renewal according to the selected checkout terms. Cancellation does not automatically refund prior charges, partial billing periods, or unused repository capacity.</p>
                <h2>5. Plan Changes and Access</h2>
                <p>Changing or cancelling a plan may affect repository limits, scans, and access to account features. We may retain certain records for audit, billing, dispute, and legal purposes.</p>
                <h2>6. Chargebacks</h2>
                <p>Please contact support before opening a payment dispute. Chargebacks may result in account suspension while the dispute is reviewed. We may provide account, checkout, access, and usage records to payment processors or banks to respond to disputes.</p>
            </section>
        <% } else { %>
            <section class="sr-legal-content">
                <h2>Do Not Sell or Share</h2>
                <p>Secure Repos and <%= appName %> do not sell personal information for money. Some analytics, advertising, attribution, or similar technologies may be considered "sharing" or "targeted advertising" under certain privacy laws.</p>
                <p>You may request to opt out by emailing <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a> with the subject line "Do Not Sell or Share Request." Include the email address associated with your account so we can process the request.</p>
                <p>We may need to verify your identity before completing certain privacy requests.</p>
            </section>
        <% } %>
            </div>
        </section>

        <footer class="landing-footer sr-footer compact-footer">
            <div class="landing-footer-brand">
                <a class="brand" href="/" style="padding:0"><%- include('../partials/brand-logo') %></a>
                <p class="muted small">GitHub repository scanning, branch-level findings, and remediation guidance for independent developers.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="landing-footer-grid">
                <div>
                    <h3>Product</h3>
                    <a href="/demo">Demo</a>
                    <a href="/#pricing">Pricing</a>
                    <a href="/faqs">FAQ</a>
                    <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3>Legal</h3>
                    <a href="/terms">Terms</a>
                    <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
                    <a href="/refund-policy">Refund Policy</a>
                    <a href="/do-not-sell">Do Not Sell/Share</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </footer>
        <%- include('../partials/cookie-consent') %>
    </main>
    <script src="/public/js/app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
